From 8821de36b337d7242f17e6f2596bc667f40323fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cliffhall <cliff@futurescale.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 01:14:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] docs: issues-not-PRs contribution model, issue forms,
 backlog plan

Outside pull requests are turned off, as in the Inspector (decided on
#4861). CONTRIBUTING.md, AGENTS.md's Contributing section, the PR
template's banner, and the fetch and time READMEs now say so.

Add bug and feature issue forms with a server dropdown, a protocol-era
field and a client field, and a config.yml that disables blank issues and
routes security reports to the private advisory form and new servers to
the MCP Server Registry.

docs/contribution-model.md records the plan for the open outside-PR
backlog (classify, harvest into issues, close with a canned comment,
verify), which #4868's triage pass carries out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: cliffhall <cliff@futurescale.com>
